WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.640
Speaker 1: there is massive, massive blowback&nbsp;
now against Dr. Anthony Fauci, the director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:15.280
of the NIH, because he said yesterday it would&nbsp;
be reasonable to require proof of vaccination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:20.960
to fly domestically right now to fly back to&nbsp;
the United States, you need a negative test&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:27.440
to fly and depending on where you're coming from,&nbsp;
vaccination to go to other countries, you often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:33.440
need vaccination. But there is no domestic airline&nbsp;
vaccine requirement right now. It's something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.000
that's been talked about for a while. Dr. Fauci,&nbsp;
without saying he's recommending it, without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.600
saying it's going to happen, in fact saying it's&nbsp;
probably not going to happen, said well, wouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:49.440
be an unreasonable thing to do. He appeared&nbsp;
on CNN yesterday and was asked about this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.480
and he answered the question. Let's take a look.
Speaker 2: Will you recommend to President Biden?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.480 --> 00:01:02.000
There should be a requirement for vaccination for&nbsp;
domestic travel. You know, I'm not going to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.480
you that for the simple reason is that I don't&nbsp;
want to be publicly telling what I'm recommending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.560
to the president because if then the president&nbsp;
doesn't do it, I don't want to make it. Look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:17.280
he's going against that. The president makes all&nbsp;
recommendations, all discussions. And as a group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.000
we make a decision about what's best to do.&nbsp;
There are pros and cons to that. I mean, you've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.920
got to ask yourself why it is. You're making that&nbsp;
requirement if you're making it a requirement for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:33.120
vaccination for people to get on planes who were&nbsp;
coming into the country, that's understandable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.560
You don't want to bring more cases into the&nbsp;
country. But if you're talking about requiring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.480
vaccination to get on a plane domestically,&nbsp;
that is just another one of the requirements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.000
that I think is reasonable to consider. And&nbsp;
I think that's what you're talking about when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.320
you heard me make a comment. You know, there's&nbsp;
requirements that you might want to get if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:57.440
want to get into college where you want to go to&nbsp;
a university or you want to work in certain places&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.040
when you make vaccination a&nbsp;
requirement, that's another incentive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.760
to get more people vaccinated. If you want to&nbsp;
do that with domestic flights, I think that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.840
something that seriously should be considered.
Speaker 1: So he says it should be considered and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:16.800
it's reasonable, and people went absolutely crazy&nbsp;
about authoritarian Foushee. Now in a moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:23.440
I'll talk about that requirement. But he&nbsp;
even said after the controversy exploded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:29.120
it it's not a likely thing to actually&nbsp;
happen. So this was later on CNN after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.680
controversy blew up. Let's take a quick look.
Speaker 2: Everything when that comes up as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:38.800
possibility, we put it on the table and we&nbsp;
consider it. That does not mean that it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.840
going to be likely to happen right now. I don't&nbsp;
think people should expect that we're going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:49.440
have a requirement in domestic flights for people&nbsp;
to be vaccinated. When I was asked that question.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:59.040
I gave an honest answer. It's on the table. OK, so
Speaker 1: what is actually logical here in terms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:06.480
of what might be achieved with such a domestic&nbsp;
airline travel mandate? I am actually ready to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:13.600
we are unlikely to vaccinate our way out&nbsp;
of the pandemic at this current point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:22.800
because Omicron is both so contagious&nbsp;
and has a significant amount of vaccine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:30.320
evasion. If we got to 100 percent vaccination,&nbsp;
maybe, but the point of the vaccines right now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:38.720
is to keep people from getting very sick. Omicron,&nbsp;
it appears, is less severe. And what that means,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:43.680
we have to be very specific about what we mean,&nbsp;
but it means that as an individual Omicron,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:50.080
if you are vaccinated. It is likely to cause&nbsp;
less serious illness than Delta, it seems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:55.280
right now. But if you are unvaccinated, you are&nbsp;
still quite likely to get very, very sick from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:02.160
Omicron. So the point of a vaccine requirement&nbsp;
to get on planes in my mind would not be to end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:06.400
cases because it doesn't seem like that's what it&nbsp;
would do. But it would be to prevent people from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.480
getting really sick and to prevent the medical&nbsp;
system from getting overloaded to that point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:17.440
Minnesota emergency physician Andrea Rowland&nbsp;
Fisher says the people ending up in the ICU&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.440
are overwhelmingly unvaccinated and
Speaker 3: folks that are vaccinated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.160
and unvaccinated. What's the kind of breakdown&nbsp;
from your estimation of what you've been seeing?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:32.720
